---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import portrait from '../../assets/ashmit-portrait.png';
---
<Layout>
  <div class="container">
    <header class="introduction" id="about">
      <div id="background">
        <p class="affiliation">Computer Science · NYU Abu Dhabi</p>
        <h1>Ashmit Mukherjee</h1>
        <p>I study how AI advice shapes people’s decisions and whether simulations can predict how groups behave.</p>
        <div class="intro-links"><a href="mailto:asm8879@nyu.edu">asm8879@nyu.edu</a><a href="https://github.com/Ansester" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a></div>
      </div>
      <Image class="portrait" src={portrait} alt="Ashmit Mukherjee" width={144} height={144} format="webp" loading="eager" />
    </header>

    <section class="home-section" id="research" aria-labelledby="research-heading">
      <h2 id="research-heading">Research</h2>
      <article class="research-entry">
        <h3><a href="/work/human-ai-collaboration/">Human–AI collaboration</a></h3>
        <p class="byline">Faculty mentors at NYU Abu Dhabi · Professors <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=GAxIreYAAAAJ">Benjamin Rosche</a> and <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=9lTiKjwAAAAJ">Hanan Salam</a></p>
        <p>I built the platform for our experiments on AI advice and cooperation, and I lead its development. Researchers can replay a game to see what advice each participant received, what they did next, and how much they earned.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="research-entry">
        <h3><a href="/work/synthetic-pilot-lab/">Synthetic Pilot Lab</a></h3>
        <p class="byline">Independent computer science capstone · 2026</p>
        <p>For my capstone, I tested how well language models predict the effect of punishment on group earnings across 20 public-goods game designs. I also built a simulator to test whether having the models play the games improves their forecasts.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="research-entry" id="manuscript">
        <h3><a href="/work/protein-language-models/">Bio-LoRA and protein models</a></h3>
        <p class="byline">eBRAIN Lab · Co-first author, November 2026 manuscript (unpublished)</p>
        <p>I developed training and evaluation pipelines for signal-peptide prediction and compared protein-model adaptation methods. In separate follow-up work, I tested residue-level biological features alongside LoRA.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="research-entry">
        <h3><a href="/work/biosynthesis-paper-database/">Biosynthesis paper database</a></h3>
        <p class="byline">eBRAIN Lab · Project led by <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=USe518cAAAAJ">Minghao Shao</a>, with Professor <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=xSR276UAAAAJ">Muhammad Shafique</a> as faculty lead</p>
        <p>I built the pipeline that collected 139,011 OpenAlex records for a biosynthesis database in November 2026. The lipid search also returned papers on signalling, which made its raw count a poor measure of biosynthesis coverage.</p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section" id="projects" aria-labelledby="projects-heading">
      <div class="section-heading" id="experience"><h2 id="projects-heading">Other projects</h2><a href="/work/">All projects ↗</a></div>
      <p>My team, SegfaultObservers (Team MENA), won the <a href="/work/csaw-llm-ctf/">CSAW 2026 LLM-CTF</a>. I built and ran the six-agent setup we used to solve challenges in parallel and check the answers.</p>
      <p>I co-developed <a href="/work/roomwise/">RoomWise</a> to help people talk through furniture choices, swipe through listings, and see each selection in a room preview. <a href="/work/fieldlens/">FieldLens</a> is a local-model tool I built for querying incident records and checking the sources behind an answer.</p>
    </section>

  </div>
</Layout>
